  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "\\(25\\times12=25\\times4\\times3=300\\).\n\nAlternative method 1: Split into tens and ones\n\nSince \\(12=10+2\\), split the product into ten groups and two groups of 25. By the distributive property,\n\\[\n25\\times12=25\\times10+25\\times2=250+50=300.\n\\]\nThe result is \\(300\\), choice C.",
